File: cmd/resubscribe/main.go (13441 bytes)

Architecture:
  - Reuses internal/tesla/client_fleet_telemetry.go's SubscribeFleetTelemetry
    via a 'pusher' interface (covenant: no new HTTP client).
  - Reuses internal/tesla/config.Builder for canonical SubscriptionFields()
    + BuildSubscription() (deterministic field list + sha256-stable bytes).
  - Reuses internal/database.VehicleRepo.GetAll for vehicle list via a
    'vehicleLister' interface so tests inject without a real DB.
  - Reuses internal/config.Load for cfg.FleetTelemetry.{Host,Port},
    cfg.Database, cfg.Tesla.

Operator credential gate (REQUIRED per covenant):
  if strings.TrimSpace(getenv(operatorTokenEnv)) == "" { ... return 1 }
  Env var: TESLASYNC_OPERATOR_TOKEN
  Behavior: refuses to run with an explicit error log line; presence-only,
  no cryptographic validation.

Audit trail (REQUIRED per covenant):
  Start line:  event=resubscribe.start, operator, vehicle_count, dry_run, workers, config_sha256
  End line:    event=resubscribe.end, succeeded, failed, skipped, duration_seconds, exit_code
  Sink: zerolog INFO -> stdout (and any configured structured sink)

Bounded worker pool:
  jobs := make(chan *models.Vehicle, rc.workers)
  for i := 0; i < rc.workers; i++ { go func() { for v := range jobs { ... } }() }
  Default workers=4, configurable via --workers flag.
  Per-call ctx, cancel := context.WithTimeout(ctx, perVehicleTimeout)

Flags:
  --dry-run                log without calling Tesla
  --vehicle <id>           single-vehicle mode for triage (0 = all)
  --workers <N>            bounded pool size (default 4)
  --per-vehicle-timeout    Tesla call timeout (default 60s)
  --version                print version and exit

Exit semantics:
  0  => every vehicle succeeded
  1  => any failure or skip (failed.Load() > 0 || skipped.Load() > 0)
  2  => flag parse error

Signal handling:
  ctx wraps signal.NotifyContext(SIGINT, SIGTERM); job dispatch select-cases
  ctx.Done() so SIGINT increments skipped counter rather than panicking.

